From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:16:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/56] Change history: mark changed lines in the gutter

Like Notepad++ "Change History": a thin bar left of the line numbers
shows which lines changed since the file was opened. Orange (theme
warning colour): changed and not saved yet. Green (theme success
colour): changed and saved in this session. Lines deleted above a line
show as a short tick at its top. Without line numbers the bar sits at
the left edge.

Marks come from a line diff (similar, Myers with a 50 ms deadline) of
three texts: the text when the tab was opened, the text at the last
save and the buffer, so undoing back to the saved text clears orange.
A restored session draft shows orange against the file on disk; an
untitled tab diffs against empty text; reloading from disk clears all
marks. The diff runs off the UI thread, 200 ms after the last edit
(500 ms for files over 1 MB), only for the visible tab, and is skipped
when the text has not changed since the last diff.

Settings > Change history > "Show changed lines" (config key
change_history, on by default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

